# Runtime of the `cuda12` variant (NVIDIA, CUDA 12). Compiled into lockfiles/cuda12.txt by
# scripts/compile_lockfiles.py; edit here, never in the .txt.
#
# * CTranslate2 (pulled in by faster-whisper) is the PyPI wheel. It carries its own CUDA runtime and loads only
#   libcublas.so.12 and libcuda.so.1 (the driver) at run time, so cuBLAS comes from a pip wheel below.
# * onnxruntime-gpu runs the VAD on the GPU. Its 1.27 and newer releases are built for CUDA 13, hence the cap.
#   Python 3.10 stops at 1.23: 1.24 publishes no cp310 wheel although its metadata allows it.
#   The cuda and cudnn extras pull the CUDA 12 libraries it dlopens (cuDNN 9, cuFFT, cuRAND, NVRTC, cudart).
#   scripts/compile_lockfiles.py leaves the CPU `onnxruntime` that faster-whisper depends on out of the lockfile:
#   both wheels install the same `onnxruntime` package and must never be present together.
# * cuBLAS stays below 12.8, the first release with Blackwell kernels; the cuda12-blackwell variant has them.
numpy>=1.26
faster-whisper>=1.1,<2
onnxruntime-gpu[cuda,cudnn]>=1.21,<1.24; python_version < "3.11"
onnxruntime-gpu[cuda,cudnn]>=1.21,<1.27; python_version >= "3.11"
nvidia-cublas-cu12<12.8
